{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})-\\int (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555/selection/c16ab704f07fd8a200175ad8c095074ed1357fb49d2d6e832cd7e66bf4fdd65d" :answer/id #uuid "3bc6ee36-3b03-5351-8102-7e2618eb170b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555/selection/028213f00724a8e309da1a80aa5c0ee53c448c8dc69928953f7187a6b72913e2" :answer/id #uuid "72777a21-401f-5678-9b00-c73119d4e69a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555/selection/9c08bb09ea9710bae2454a5397cfc71b636212f76665e9d988d1c7b86bfd9f7e" :answer/id #uuid "dda2229a-76c1-5f0d-ab3a-4ac41fa9ac53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555/selection/7b081373917d329c8ae1d4fd483e182b6208d92a4b0bf87b2158e94faa3f946e" :answer/id #uuid "f602bd11-ba18-5d65-80f8-e2972b3cabbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555/selection/5e7dd8d90ada518b74b303a6c8ce47fd215f141f8a8c11676d5f0fd2d6881f29" :answer/id #uuid "133ed4fd-7ae8-5543-8c8f-0d689e1c9f57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a75af52e-b616-5efd-9d80-047070c42974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114555/selection/5e7dd8d90ada518b74b303a6c8ce47fd215f141f8a8c11676d5f0fd2d6881f29" :answer-field/choices ["q-114555/selection/c16ab704f07fd8a200175ad8c095074ed1357fb49d2d6e832cd7e66bf4fdd65d" "q-114555/selection/028213f00724a8e309da1a80aa5c0ee53c448c8dc69928953f7187a6b72913e2" "q-114555/selection/9c08bb09ea9710bae2454a5397cfc71b636212f76665e9d988d1c7b86bfd9f7e" "q-114555/selection/7b081373917d329c8ae1d4fd483e182b6208d92a4b0bf87b2158e94faa3f946e" "q-114555/selection/5e7dd8d90ada518b74b303a6c8ce47fd215f141f8a8c11676d5f0fd2d6881f29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114555" :question/id #uuid "7fe9b973-85cd-5569-aae4-2db535d24d76" :question/math-academy-id "q-114555" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=8{x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 8{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\cdot (2{x}^{4})-\\int \\frac{2{x}^{4}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114555/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114555"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556/selection/c0d0d603796dc0d1d9b4c5dabf4c17307d4f6a9b7ba2e1ee8d3642821fd137eb" :answer/id #uuid "4ba52cda-c7be-5591-a551-1a8aca9e19bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556/selection/fec1f560bced8d5de2a93b43d4bd784d24031b9ecd088b27c716cecd46cbb113" :answer/id #uuid "40e0240f-2655-5b8d-956c-6b0ceb344a06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556/selection/eb52d67b85ca57ec34e5f1ddc0489feb669352fffa35e143af9675b13f478829" :answer/id #uuid "839ff85f-c34c-5c3c-b037-815079fd6655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556/selection/1e47979900e9234d5255cd75e080f7b6f17430663d21ed76d909d10e01865770" :answer/id #uuid "8193345e-f5e5-5582-9492-3d0696344172" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556/selection/0d54478fd06bec4b806a27312ba2d04ab0b2cb9605cf537b0de269c6e378940b" :answer/id #uuid "19e32fa8-90ab-5f78-a1da-cf421141cb00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eeb504cb-d712-53f5-9c85-be74cc3f59eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114556/selection/0d54478fd06bec4b806a27312ba2d04ab0b2cb9605cf537b0de269c6e378940b" :answer-field/choices ["q-114556/selection/c0d0d603796dc0d1d9b4c5dabf4c17307d4f6a9b7ba2e1ee8d3642821fd137eb" "q-114556/selection/fec1f560bced8d5de2a93b43d4bd784d24031b9ecd088b27c716cecd46cbb113" "q-114556/selection/eb52d67b85ca57ec34e5f1ddc0489feb669352fffa35e143af9675b13f478829" "q-114556/selection/1e47979900e9234d5255cd75e080f7b6f17430663d21ed76d909d10e01865770" "q-114556/selection/0d54478fd06bec4b806a27312ba2d04ab0b2cb9605cf537b0de269c6e378940b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114556" :question/id #uuid "a4eb688e-c5f1-5e1b-a808-764b83388ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114556" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114556/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579/selection/60b10a6f1a60bc696df4de3596c76c3f420c0bf5c805900b3dbe7d3266deb20e" :answer/id #uuid "9fec5b92-742f-5131-b6ee-8697e0573919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579/selection/f2fc2cc07504afdd68e686625424b1405ea4b430eb761e4487018258c30e2d7f" :answer/id #uuid "ddf8ad37-97c5-52c4-9f50-a7d3b497740a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579/selection/897be9a3b1306843243248a40069ec4eacd9663611b755927ae7821160d033e2" :answer/id #uuid "fa4d5c0b-b085-55f3-bba7-69a470201edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-\\frac{x}{3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579/selection/19c7adb597ece9e3534f876d45f151d3f462a6f7db12ea369c1f2d47f1ae3be3" :answer/id #uuid "4c0aef57-abe2-5e9b-8ffd-b4ac250e8856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579/selection/fe915a8078ad9f4fd68e9ac45f2454a4e25528f3f7701435b2af91543b6f64cf" :answer/id #uuid "260a2b08-273c-5530-b4b4-c3d9f234169d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "507e7950-22fa-5522-8d6e-e608954b5950" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114579/selection/fe915a8078ad9f4fd68e9ac45f2454a4e25528f3f7701435b2af91543b6f64cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-114579/selection/60b10a6f1a60bc696df4de3596c76c3f420c0bf5c805900b3dbe7d3266deb20e" "q-114579/selection/f2fc2cc07504afdd68e686625424b1405ea4b430eb761e4487018258c30e2d7f" "q-114579/selection/897be9a3b1306843243248a40069ec4eacd9663611b755927ae7821160d033e2" "q-114579/selection/19c7adb597ece9e3534f876d45f151d3f462a6f7db12ea369c1f2d47f1ae3be3" "q-114579/selection/fe915a8078ad9f4fd68e9ac45f2454a4e25528f3f7701435b2af91543b6f64cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114579" :question/id #uuid "df4a8ff9-b6f1-509e-8da7-ab67f79ced45" :question/math-academy-id "q-114579" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114579/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114579"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585/selection/7c7b8baeb1dc890fd1b0622fd237f1d46ab11b2921bc89917c4de16f6af55c79" :answer/id #uuid "4c9bb09f-ba9a-558b-a38f-4a830e721b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585/selection/682d5f01c8705151c448abe6426ae2523633e1c161371dfc29146e0d9c9ad1e0" :answer/id #uuid "da8e5247-bf52-58e7-975b-3f66820670b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585/selection/78fc64f9c42f1488f0a0a28c0de575c0cf15d119f261e24fbd70e7c23f68af26" :answer/id #uuid "7c70f475-b1d5-5e18-95d2-9e7c922f108d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585/selection/a84a88a01fffbd2a63f31eebf904379928e7a7cdfbdbed20f2dd940fbac6aaab" :answer/id #uuid "01007e7f-0a9b-5ac6-b36d-8e9f915bf27f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585/selection/ad44e08331e36e359061b003681bac6e8724aeeb99fb3b0032015ea402f1ec00" :answer/id #uuid "79dfeb14-bf2b-5497-bb34-51386778e9d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db580e37-a8f2-560e-b595-86510254902c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114585/selection/a84a88a01fffbd2a63f31eebf904379928e7a7cdfbdbed20f2dd940fbac6aaab" :answer-field/choices ["q-114585/selection/7c7b8baeb1dc890fd1b0622fd237f1d46ab11b2921bc89917c4de16f6af55c79" "q-114585/selection/682d5f01c8705151c448abe6426ae2523633e1c161371dfc29146e0d9c9ad1e0" "q-114585/selection/78fc64f9c42f1488f0a0a28c0de575c0cf15d119f261e24fbd70e7c23f68af26" "q-114585/selection/a84a88a01fffbd2a63f31eebf904379928e7a7cdfbdbed20f2dd940fbac6aaab" "q-114585/selection/ad44e08331e36e359061b003681bac6e8724aeeb99fb3b0032015ea402f1ec00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114585" :question/id #uuid "1883a81f-d78c-537f-b99d-5e0b9aacac58" :question/math-academy-id "q-114585" :question/problem "$\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{2x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $2x+1=u,$ thus $2x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int (\\frac{2x}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{u}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡u}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{2x+1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346521/field-1/4cd6ec8258cd847bbf8ae10b93cc9e4f96e5327b82b20d4af6d729d466851bbc" :answer/id #uuid "e33c738d-a3f4-5682-833f-dbc29b7a6f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^3}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346521/field-1/2a4c844b54622d39db95dbbbbc86e02ac5f14bcfeb5b6cca40868b8674d9d0c1" :answer/id #uuid "031bf082-77a5-50b2-bbc9-0b0aae1d4c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^3}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346521/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b87aac84-1410-5551-b4fb-311889aa660e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346521/field-1/4cd6ec8258cd847bbf8ae10b93cc9e4f96e5327b82b20d4af6d729d466851bbc" :answer-field/choices ["q-346521/field-1/4cd6ec8258cd847bbf8ae10b93cc9e4f96e5327b82b20d4af6d729d466851bbc" "q-346521/field-1/2a4c844b54622d39db95dbbbbc86e02ac5f14bcfeb5b6cca40868b8674d9d0c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346521" :question/id #uuid "e48be342-f105-55aa-a661-6f4ddf44b83d" :question/math-academy-id "q-346521" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,(x){|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3}}{4})\\,(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4})\\,(\\frac{1}{4})]-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2{e}^{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-346521/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346521"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969/selection/a124276b240645959f62b12725b2c2ba6d293e81ae1052855f5ba2fa9d8dde36" :answer/id #uuid "9fa3d80c-ab19-528d-906f-c1b2436c1e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969/selection/229cb3875c21296f2503a01472d6ac3fb8152fc5d7f4c84caf31f7fe9fcb708b" :answer/id #uuid "e3521934-f36f-5ef0-b806-afdb329e3c48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969/selection/79efeeaebbbdbc24691cd06d9360573bf99554f96406a1d4470e4e5bc6c03ee2" :answer/id #uuid "93161ec1-c844-5d3c-a140-ce0ff6d366fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969/selection/2c3843592d685f4be9805bc025c4272c91519793f8de98f250bdd0e76eec664d" :answer/id #uuid "891afc57-76e7-51ca-aede-21264ec11dbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969/selection/23ecdc3f8e73bca7867c9fa3be5abad25ed800a2523ef1cdc84bd61639f8ec01" :answer/id #uuid "b7428390-750b-5084-873b-8a8b645f41a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e81f80-e4a9-5d16-b74c-78c47753826b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78969/selection/2c3843592d685f4be9805bc025c4272c91519793f8de98f250bdd0e76eec664d" :answer-field/choices ["q-78969/selection/a124276b240645959f62b12725b2c2ba6d293e81ae1052855f5ba2fa9d8dde36" "q-78969/selection/229cb3875c21296f2503a01472d6ac3fb8152fc5d7f4c84caf31f7fe9fcb708b" "q-78969/selection/79efeeaebbbdbc24691cd06d9360573bf99554f96406a1d4470e4e5bc6c03ee2" "q-78969/selection/2c3843592d685f4be9805bc025c4272c91519793f8de98f250bdd0e76eec664d" "q-78969/selection/23ecdc3f8e73bca7867c9fa3be5abad25ed800a2523ef1cdc84bd61639f8ec01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78969" :question/id #uuid "bbf7c630-44ce-52c1-83dd-093ebe2d7594" :question/math-academy-id "q-78969" :question/problem "$\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 2\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78969/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78969"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597/selection/5a12c831b52ce734bdc0e3ca129a4c5d625fb51273afafdf40c4be727e2e141c" :answer/id #uuid "2523163f-f6c8-593f-84d3-2cc72115ce70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+3e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597/selection/ed98b5bd4faf2fd3099f2a970714763d74f82489626b66003e451357c9b8e874" :answer/id #uuid "8a0193d2-3eaf-54be-ab46-a92ca0576550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597/selection/c49f46b8f1783451e7b120d73eebe3ffdbf21ac9dc993d6e1dbf173efb70e36c" :answer/id #uuid "1a2bdbe1-f3b7-5f26-82ea-a5b7f432f8ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597/selection/61d1f73870c72ce05979fca9880a86fdc7390065cf89a7de96cd30cf932d233e" :answer/id #uuid "b7142bcd-73dd-5cf7-b9e8-132f3589d839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597/selection/4b097fee6d1097f00d96273b31f97a0ab13abc5c52b7377e14d71c330bf93084" :answer/id #uuid "7705c3a4-0e35-509d-9808-fa04f351083f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ea2e213-fe2f-5dc2-9ef9-784bd287e6a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114597/selection/ed98b5bd4faf2fd3099f2a970714763d74f82489626b66003e451357c9b8e874" :answer-field/choices ["q-114597/selection/5a12c831b52ce734bdc0e3ca129a4c5d625fb51273afafdf40c4be727e2e141c" "q-114597/selection/ed98b5bd4faf2fd3099f2a970714763d74f82489626b66003e451357c9b8e874" "q-114597/selection/c49f46b8f1783451e7b120d73eebe3ffdbf21ac9dc993d6e1dbf173efb70e36c" "q-114597/selection/61d1f73870c72ce05979fca9880a86fdc7390065cf89a7de96cd30cf932d233e" "q-114597/selection/4b097fee6d1097f00d96273b31f97a0ab13abc5c52b7377e14d71c330bf93084"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114597" :question/id #uuid "61e03c45-6b55-5bc8-8f4d-4ef143900018" :question/math-academy-id "q-114597" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x){|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-x{|}_{1/3}^{e}\\, \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-(e-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+e-e+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114597/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-493"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-494"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3993"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
